    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **34 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` string property for a `membershipLevel` integer (int32, min 1, max 3), documenting the create-time formula. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getMembershipLevel()` and drops the old field from the response schema.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 replaced the tier expression with the level computation: `Math.min(3, 1 + (email present ? 1 : 0) + (namesakeCount == 0 ? 1 : 0))`. Both `getOwner` and `addOwner` read this back consistently from the stored `email`/`namesakeCount`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reordered the create flow so the DTO is mapped before the audit line, then extended the audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` (from `ownerDto.getMembershipLevel()`, keeping a single source of truth). Also cleaned up the stale GOLD-tier javadoc.\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 updated the `householdSize` comment that referenced the removed tier.\n\nThe level behaves as specified: base 1, +1 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (leaving 4 for tenure), and the previous household-driven GOLD tier is gone.",
